{title: Beautiful Dreamer}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: C}

{c: Verse 1}
[C]Beautiful dreamer, [G7]wake unto [C]me,
[F]Starlight and dew[C]drops are [G7]waiting for [C]thee.
[C]Sounds of the rude world [G7]heard in the [C]day,
[F]Lulled by the [C]moonlight have [G7]all passed a[C]way.

{c: Chorus}
[G7]Beautiful [C]dreamer, [G7]queen of my [C]song,
[G7]List while I [C]woo thee with [D7]soft melo[G7]dy.
[C]Beautiful dreamer, [G7]awaken to [C]me,
[F]Beautiful [C]dreamer, a[G7]waken to [C]me.

{c: Verse 2}
[C]Beautiful dreamer, [G7]out on the [C]sea,
[F]Mermaids are [C]chanting the [G7]wild lore[C]lei.
[C]Over the streamlet [G7]vapors are [C]borne,
[F]Waiting to [C]fade at the [G7]bright coming [C]morn.
